#
# The Deeper Sands batch file
# Expands Arena Sands with a real leveled continuation, gated at the
# entrance so newcomers can't wander in over their heads. Run this
# FROM Arena Sands, or let the initial @tel handle it.
#
# Rebalanced from an original level 6+ newbie-adjacent range (up to
# 25) into genuine level 75-100 endgame content, by direct request -
# the sewers (Cloaca Maxima) are the real post-Ludus leveling zone
# now, so this stopped needing to double as one. The room text below
# still describes the original tiered progression (Recruit's Circle
# through the Master's Sands) - only the ARENA_FIGHTER_* prototypes'
# own level/xp_reward/desc fields (world/prototypes.py) actually
# changed, not this file or the rooms it builds.
#
# Usage: batchcommands world.batch_deeper_sands
#
# LAST STEP (not automatable - requires being physically in the room):
# stand in Arena Sands and retype the "onward" exit into the gated
# threshold:
#   @typeclass onward = world.colosseum.DeeperSandsGateExit
#

#
@tel Arena Sands
#
@dig Threshold of the Deeper Sands = onward;o, back;b
#
onward
#
@desc here = |wThreshold of the Deeper Sands|n

The sand changes underfoot here - packed harder, darker, stained by years of fights the newbie yard never sees. A weathered sign leans against the tunnel wall, half in Latin, half in whatever the last person to read it scratched underneath: further in, further danger. This is not a place for the untested.
#
@dig Recruit's Circle = onward;o, back;b
#
onward
#
@desc here = |wRecruit's Circle|n

A modest ring, sand still fairly clean, marked out for fighters who've moved past the absolute basics but haven't yet earned the deeper sand. A green arena recruit is here, working through forms with more enthusiasm than precision.
#
py here.db.trainer_prototype = "ARENA_FIGHTER_RECRUIT"
#
@dig Hunter's Round = onward;o, back;b
#
onward
#
@desc here = |wHunter's Round|n

An open, circular yard, sand churned by hooves as much as feet. A Centaur arena hunter paces its edge, javelin never quite still, watching the tunnel mouth for whoever's next.
#
py here.db.trainer_prototype = "ARENA_FIGHTER_HUNTER"
#
@dig Brute's Pit = onward;o, back;b
#
onward
#
@desc here = |wBrute's Pit|n

A sunken ring, walls scarred deep enough to suggest the fights held here don't always stay contained to the sand. A Minotaur arena brute waits at the center, utterly still, breathing slow.
#
py here.db.trainer_prototype = "ARENA_FIGHTER_BRUTE"
#
@dig Duelist's Ring = onward;o, back;b
#
onward
#
@desc here = |wDuelist's Ring|n

A tighter, more formal space than the others - less pit, more stage. A Harpy arena duelist waits with the patient stillness of someone who has never once needed to move first.
#
py here.db.trainer_prototype = "ARENA_FIGHTER_DUELIST"
#
@dig Champion's Coliseum = onward;o, back;b
#
onward
#
@desc here = |wChampion's Coliseum|n

A proper arena in miniature, tiered stone benches rising just high enough to suggest this fight is meant to be watched, not just fought. A Cyclops arena champion stands ready at its center, shield already raised.
#
py here.db.trainer_prototype = "ARENA_FIGHTER_CHAMPION"
#
@dig The Master's Sands = onward;o, back;b
#
onward
#
@desc here = |wThe Master's Sands|n

The deepest ring, and the quietest. No benches, no crowd - just sand, and a figure standing at its center who has never once needed an audience to be dangerous. This is the Arena Master's ground, and everyone who reaches it already knows it.
#
py here.db.trainer_prototype = "ARENA_FIGHTER_MASTER"
#
back
#
back
#
back
#
back
#
back
#
back
#
back
#
# Build complete. Last step: stand in Arena Sands and run
#   @typeclass onward = world.colosseum.DeeperSandsGateExit
# to actually enforce the level 6+ gate on the threshold exit.
#
